# fibi40-client UI Review Rules

## Templates and styling

- **BLOCK:** Templates reference only public class members.
- **BLOCK:** Do not manipulate DOM with jQuery; use Angular bindings or `Renderer2`.
- **BLOCK:** Do not add static inline `style` attributes. Dynamic style bindings are allowed.
- **BLOCK:** `!important` requires a comment naming the third-party style overridden and why.
- **BLOCK:** New component style files are `.scss`, and `styleUrls` points to `.scss`.
- Object-array `*ngFor` loops require `trackBy`.
- Async views handle loading, empty, and error states.
- Move complex template expressions into the component.
- Rely on normal `[innerHTML]` sanitization. Any `bypassSecurityTrust*` use requires documented source-safety reasoning and a named reviewer.
- Define new template classes in matching component SCSS or comment the shared/global source.
- Keep component styles out of global `src/assets/css`; use class bindings instead of jQuery toggles.
- Reuse SCSS variables/CSS custom properties for repeated values; do not use ID selectors in component styles.

## Required accessibility gates

- **BLOCK:** Every image has descriptive `alt`, or `alt=""` when decorative.
- **BLOCK:** Every button has a unique `id`, `title`, and `aria-label`.
- **BLOCK:** Icon-only links and controls without visible text use `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`.
- **BLOCK:** Every form input has a visible `<label>` connected by matching `for` and `id`.
- **BLOCK:** Associate validation errors with inputs through `aria-describedby`.
- **BLOCK:** Toast/status regions use `aria-live="polite"` and `aria-atomic="true"`.
- **BLOCK:** Data tables include `<caption>` and `<th scope="col|row">`.
- **BLOCK:** Modals move and trap focus inside, then restore focus to the trigger.
- **BLOCK:** Authentication cannot rely only on a visual/cognitive puzzle; provide an accessible alternative.

## Additional accessibility

- Clickable `div`/`span` elements support Enter and Space and have an appropriate role and `tabindex`.
- Text contrast is at least 4.5:1, or 3:1 for 18pt/14pt-bold large text.
- Click targets are at least 24×24 CSS pixels.
- Sticky/fixed UI cannot fully obscure focused elements.
- Never remove focus outlines without a replacement at least 2px wide with 3:1 contrast.
- Drag interactions need click or keyboard alternatives.
- Animations over five seconds can be paused/stopped/hidden or respect reduced-motion preferences.
- Keep heading hierarchy sequential and preserve non-empty `<html lang="en">`.

## Internationalisation

- New user-facing text uses `i18n`; translated attributes use `i18n-<attribute>`.
